      "id": "claim_7e81654961ba4ae98e6f0a6721e0ee98",
      "statement": "Express and Fastify defer to their framework-derived `req.ip` or `request.ip` when WebDecoy `trustProxy` is unset, whereas Next.js Edge middleware and the generic fetch guard default to one trusted hop because they do not have a portable socket peer; Next.js Pages API protection uses the Node peer and no forwarding trust by default.",
