      "id": "claim_4f10ed41e71340cf8456c1f83f82c72c",
      "statement": "Edge verdict headers are advisory rather than authentication and can safely drive application behavior only when every origin request is forced through the validator that strips inbound copies; direct or bypass requests can forge headers, and absence is no information.",
