      "statement": "WebDecoy parses edge context into every rule context and attaches it to every `protect()` decision; filter expressions expose `edge.present`, `edge.class`, clearance, and predicates, while Next.js exposes `getEdgeVerdict()` for request/header sources and forwards edge tags to application request headers rather than browser response headers.",
